      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The yeast ferments sugars in the flour, producing carbon dioxide gas, which is what causes the dough to rise. Simultaneously, the lactobacilli consume sugars and produce lactic and acetic acids. These acids are responsible for the characteristic sour flavor of sourdough, while the gas from the yeast provides the necessary leavening action. This symbiotic relationship between the yeast and bacteria is essential for both the texture and taste of sourdough bread.",
