      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While both thrive in the sourdough environment, there isn't typically a direct, antagonistic \"battle\" where one outright kills the other in a healthy starter. Instead, they rely on a competitive balance within the dough's matrix. High acidity, produced by the lactobacilli, can inhibit the growth of unwanted molds and pathogens, effectively \"keeping things stable.\" This community dynamic allows them to co-exist and perform their complementary functions.",
